FIX FE RESULTS/SEASON MENUS (824): reconstruct post-race + championship-standings dispatch

Comprehensive scan of ALL FE main-table-style dispatch tables (stride-20, code=int() sites)
found SIX post-race/season menus with unregistered raw-VA handlers + void-typed handlers that
would trap on wasm the moment a race COMPLETES (or the pause->quit/results path is taken):
  Practice_Over @0x46a53c, @0x46a7fc, @0x46aaa8, @0x46af78, Race_Over @0x46b7cc, season @0x46c064.
Same unreconstructed-handler + int-typing class as View Statistics/Sound/CD (821-823) and 818.

Reconstructed 1:1 from objdump of dd2h.exe (20 handlers): the Save Replay / Quit / Next Race /
Total Destruction / View League / View Replay / File Options / View Statistics label thunks +
confirm/return actions, the shared standings VIEWER 0x453c00 (index @0x46ad00 0..3, LEFT/RIGHT
cycle, 0x1000 exit), the race_type-branched setups 0x4545e8 / 0x45595c-family (store the live
0x454b80|0x453c00 handler into 0x46c07c/0x46af90 per race_type @0x4673f4), and the tiny
save-replay helpers 0x44ab74 / 0x44ad88. All 20 table handlers registered in dd2_dispatch.c.

Also int-widened 10 EXISTING void-typed registered handlers in these tables (FUN_00452ef0 /
453b90 / 453bb0 / 454318 / 4543a8 / 454438 / 4544c8 / 454558 / 45505c / 4558ec) -- a void
setup traps the code=int() call_indirect (patch-818 class).

Found by a static sweep of every (&PTR_FUN_00XXXX)[uVarN*5] dispatch site's handler slots vs the
fnmap (tools: scan). Regression: verify + verify-wasm 10/10 both; native<->wasm L9 702/702
bit-identical.

